# Architecture Rules

See root `AGENTS.md` for the full brief.

## Critical constraints

- Anything regulatory (VAT rates, allergen lists, DAC7 thresholds) MUST come
  from `packages/compliance/src/`. Never hardcode these values in `apps/`.
- Shared TypeScript types live in `packages/types/src/`. Do not duplicate
  product/seller/order shapes between web and mobile.
- `apps/web` uses Next.js Pages Router with `output: 'export'` for GitHub Pages.
  Do not introduce App Router patterns without migrating the whole app.
- Server-side secrets (Stripe secret key, Auth0 client secret) must never appear
  in client bundles. Use server actions or API routes only.
- Leave `// COMPLIANCE-REVIEW:` comments on any line that implements regulatory
  logic that needs legal verification before going live.
